# Motif menu keyboard-navigation differential for PR-73 ("you can't navigate
# with arrows reliably ... down just causes the menu to close"). Drives the
# self-contained menu-nav-test.c app: post the File pulldown, then press Down
# and require the menu to stay posted. Under the old low-byte keycode mapping
# Down (SDLK_DOWN 0x40000051) truncated to keycode 0x51 and aliased onto Q, so
# Motif never saw osfDown and the traversal action collapsed the menu.
#
# xdotool backend ONLY: the Down/Escape codes below map to xdotool keysym names
# in scripts/run-ui-replay.py (replay_keysym), not to the internal replay engine
# which reads the arg as an X keycode. Run each side on node11 (needs Xvfb,
# xdotool, ImageMagick import, and Motif); the system-libX11 build is the ground
# truth and the libx11-compat build must reach the same PASS:
#
#   cc ... menu-nav-test.c <system-or-compat libXm/libXt/libX11> -o menu-nav
#   python3 scripts/run-ui-replay.py --app ./menu-nav \
#       --replay tests/ui/replays/motif-menu-nav.replay \
#       --input-backend xdotool --xvfb --display 121 --geometry 1000x700 \
#       --screenshot-command import --out-root /tmp/menunav-<side>
#
# CALIBRATION: motif-menu-nav-posted.json compares the whole frame, so it is
# position independent, but its min_changed_ratio is a first estimate. On the
# first node11 run read screens/posted.png vs screens/after-down.png and set the
# threshold to sit between "pulldown present" and "pulldown gone".
delay 2000
wait-window "MenuNav" 8000
# Fixed settle rather than wait-converge: that primitive drives the
# libx11-compat event loop and has no meaning on the system-libX11 ground-truth
# side, so a cross-runtime differential must not use it.
delay 2500
screenshot initial

# Post the File pulldown. target-motion is window-relative, so it does not
# depend on where SDL or the server placed the top-level. File sits at the left
# of the menu bar.
target-motion 20 14
delay 50
button 1 press
delay 300
screenshot posted

# The reported failure: the first Down collapses the menu instead of moving into
# it. Traverse twice with the button still held, matching the reporter who
# navigated with the button down. 1073741905 is SDLK_DOWN; replay_keysym in
# run-ui-replay.py maps it to the xdotool "Down" keysym.
key 1073741905
delay 150
key 1073741905
delay 200
screenshot after-down
assert-image after-down motif-menu-nav-posted.json

# Negative control plus cleanup: Escape (27 == SDLK_ESCAPE) dismisses the menu,
# then release the button.
key 27
delay 150
button 1 release
